{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the magicians said to Pharaoh.</b> Until now, 'the magicians' (החרטמים) has been written plene with a yod, but in this plague of lice, where it says ולא יכלו, it writes החרטמם defectively without a yod, because here their wisdom failed and their strength faltered, and they admitted against their will. Furthermore, the missing yod alludes to what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: ten measures of sorcery descended to the world — Egypt took nine, and one the entire world." "<b>It is the finger of Elohim.</b> When the magicians saw that they could not bring forth the lice, they acknowledged that Aaron's deed was from Elohim. Therefore Pharaoh did not summon them from this time onward. And in order to minimize the matter they said ״אצבע אלהים״ — 'the finger of Elohim,' that is, a small plague from Him, and they did not say ״אצבע ה׳״ — 'the finger of YHWH,' because Pharaoh and his servants would not mention the distinctive Name, except when speaking with Moses, for he would mention it to them. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>But.</b> The sage R. ibn Ezra, of blessed memory, wrote that their saying ״אצבע אלהים היא״ — 'it is the finger of Elohim' — is not an acknowledgment that they conceded Aaron's deed was divine; rather, they said that this plague did not come through the power of Moses and Aaron on behalf of Israel, but through the power of the stars and constellations this plague was fitting to come upon the land of Egypt. And for this reason they mentioned the name Elohim and did not say ״אצבע ה׳״ — the finger of YHWH, who is the God of Israel. And there is further proof: He warned him regarding the plague of blood and the plague of frogs, but did not warn him regarding the plague of lice. Therefore they told him that it did not come through the power of Moses from HaShem, blessed be He, but according to the configuration of the stars over the earth, and Moses did not know this, and therefore did not warn him." "<b>And know</b> that in the first two plagues, namely blood and frogs, there was no new creation, for the plague of blood was a transformation of the water into blood, and the frogs came up from the river — which is why Scripture says ותעל הצפרדע, for they gathered and came up, and it did not say ויהיו הצפרדעים. But the lice involved a new creation, and therefore it says והיה לכנים, and it also says להוציא את הכנים, in the manner of (Genesis 1:24) ״תוצא הארץ נפש חיה״ — ״ויהי כן.״ And the power to create any creature belongs to no one in creation except HaShem alone. Therefore Scripture used the expression 'finger,' whose meaning is 'wonder,' as in the expression used of the celestial spheres (Psalms 8:4): ״מעשה אצבעותיך״ — 'the work of Your fingers,' for the creation of the celestial sphere is, relative to His power, blessed be He, as slight as the creation of a gnat. And thus R. Saadia Gaon wrote: we find the expression 'finger' in three things — in the celestial spheres, in the tablets, and in the plague of lice. The celestial sphere is at the extremity of greatness, with no body above it; the tablets are below it in corporeality but above it in brilliance; the lice are at the extremity of smallness and lowliness. And despite this, Scripture used one expression for all three, to indicate that everything is one and equal before His power, blessed be He. And the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory in the Midrash regarding what is stated, ״ולא יכולו,״ is that a demon has no dominion over a creature smaller than a lentil. If so, there is no need to say that they had no power to create them — rather, even to gather them and bring them from their place they had no power, because they are smaller than a lentil."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {2 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:09.060753500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}